Vendored secret-detection rules
===============================

apps/docs/redaction/secret-rules.json is derived from the default gitleaks rule set.

  Project:   gitleaks (https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks)
  Source:    config/gitleaks.toml
  Tag:       v8.30.1
  Commit:    83d9cd684c87d95d656c1458ef04895a7f1cbd8e
  SHA-256:   e163e53b9e7e8a8511e77271e2b323ed057759542a6d988258afe3a1fa329caf (of config/gitleaks.toml at that commit)
  Retrieved: 2026-11-01
  License:   MIT (text below)

Conversion
----------

Each [[rules]] entry became one JSON object: id, regex, and the optional flags, secretGroup, entropy and
keywords fields. The gate honors keywords (a rule runs only if one appears in the text), the secret group
and the entropy floor. Dropped: descriptions, per-rule [[rules.allowlists]], path filters, the global
[allowlist], and tags.

The Go (RE2) patterns were translated for JavaScript:
  - A leading (?i), (?s) or (?m) group became the RegExp flag.
  - Named groups (?P<name>...) became (?<name>...), and \z became $.
  - Inline modifier groups, (?i), (?i:...) and (?-i:...) in mid-pattern, are not supported by the runtime.
    They were lifted to the whole pattern: any 'i' makes the entire rule case-insensitive. That is a
    superset of the original matches, which suits a redaction gate, but it can over-report.
    Rules affected: adobe-client-secret, alibaba-access-key-id, atlassian-api-token,
    authress-service-client-access-key, cisco-meraki-api-key, cohere-api-token, curl-auth-header,
    doppler-api-token, duffel-api-token, dynatrace-api-token, easypost-api-token, easypost-test-api-token,
    etsy-access-token, facebook-page-access-token, flutterwave-encryption-key, flutterwave-public-key,
    flutterwave-secret-key, frameio-api-token, gocardless-api-token, hashicorp-tf-api-token,
    huggingface-access-token, huggingface-organization-api-token, intra42-client-secret,
    kubernetes-secret-yaml, linear-api-key, okta-access-token, planetscale-api-token, planetscale-password,
    postman-api-token, privateai-api-token, sendgrid-api-token, sendinblue-api-token, sumologic-access-id,
    sumologic-access-token, telegram-bot-api-token, vault-service-token.

Excluded rules
--------------

  generic-api-key   The generic high-entropy rule. It matches any key-looking assignment and needs
                    allowlists and stopwords that this snapshot drops.
  pkcs12-file       A path-only rule with no content regex.

Every other rule in the tag compiles in JavaScript after the translation above (220 of 222 rules kept).

To refresh: fetch config/gitleaks.toml at a newer tag, repeat the conversion, update this file, and run
the gate over the corpus.

